  "worked_solution": "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3+3+4 & 6-1+2 & 3+2+0 \\\\ 4-3+10 & 8+1+5 & 4-2+0 \\\\ 2+0+6 & 4+0+3 & 2+0+0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 11 & 14 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
